  "summary_md": "**ヒガナヨガナ ([@higana_yogana](https://x.com/higana_yogana/status/2116146468868469215))** reviews **snapref** in an 8-part thread, a node and LoRA inspired by Anima-Ref-Adapter that references only a character's features: options include a speed/accuracy toggle, char vs char+style modes, Spectrum and Turbo LoRA support and wide negative strength (e.g. -1.0 to force monochrome); prompts, not ref_caption, carry artist tags, and it combines with CharRef-LLLite ControlNet though prompting is needed to use shapes ([0ppxnhximxr/snapref-v1b](https://huggingface.co/0ppxnhximxr/snapref-v1b)). A later follow-up adds that Spectrum requires turning ref_guidance_on off, and that SnapRef v2a preview builds (pre1 and pre2) are now out, linking to the author's own impressions of pre2.",
